## Comprehensive Report: About Page Scene/Proof/Section Code Architecture

I've thoroughly explored the Three.js/TypeScript about page project. Here are the key findings:

### 1. **Core File Locations**

| File | Path |
|------|------|
| Main About Scene Config | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/about/scene/about.scene.ts` |
| Proof Renderer | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/about/render/AboutProofRenderer.ts` |
| Gallery Renderer | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/about/render/InfiniteGalleryRenderer.ts` |
| Theatre Runtime | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/about/theatre/AboutTheatreRuntime.ts` |
| Proof Rotation Strategy | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/about/render/ProofRotationStrategy.ts` |
| Page Runtime | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/about/runtime/AboutPageRuntime.ts` |
| Theatre Config | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/about/theatre/AboutTheatreConfig.ts` |
| Scene Runtime | `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/runtime/ScrollSceneRuntime.ts` |

---

### 2. **"no-sub-about" and "no-sub-about-section" Pattern**

These are **HTML/CSS class selectors** used to identify sections on the about page (not TypeScript constructs):

**In HTML** (`/views/pages/about/index.php`):
- `.no-sub-about-proof` — container for proof section (canvas + scenes)
- `.no-sub-about-proof__canvas-wrap` — wraps canvas element
- `.no-sub-about-proof__scene` — individual proof scene cards
- `.no-sub-about-proof__pin` — content pin within each scene
- `.no-sub-about-section` — wrapper class for all about sections

**In TypeScript** (`about.scene.ts`, lines 308-318):
```typescript
const ABOUT_SCROLL_SCENE_SELECTORS: SceneSelectorMap<AboutSceneSectionKey> = {
  heroIntro: '.no-sub-about-hero-intro[data-scene="heroIntro"]',
  heroSlogan: '.no-sub-about-hero-slogan[data-scene="heroSlogan"]',
  gallery: '.no-sub-about-gallery[data-scene="gallery"]',
  proof: '.no-sub-about-proof[data-scene="proof"]',  // ← Proof selector
  // ... other sections
}
```

---

### 3. **"scene-shell" Concept**

**What it is:** A CSS class + SCSS variable system that controls the **scroll span height** for each scene section.

**Key locations:**

**SCSS Variables** (`resource/scss/base/_root.scss`, line 28):
```scss
--scene-shell-span: 100vh;  // Default 100 viewport height units
```

**Applied by ScrollSceneRuntime** (`resource/ts/runtime/ScrollSceneRuntime.ts`, lines 414-427):
```typescript
private _applySceneShell(
  element: HTMLElement,
  scrollSpanVh: number,
): () => void {
  const shellClass = "scene-shell";
  element.classList.add(shellClass);
  element.style.setProperty("--scene-shell-span", `${scrollSpanVh}vh`);
  return () => {
    element.classList.remove(shellClass);
    element.style.removeProperty("--scene-shell-span");
  };
}
```

**Configuration in about.scene.ts** (lines 352-359):
```typescript
proof: {
  ...ABOUT_TOP_ANCHORED_SCENE_OPTION,
  scrollSpanVh: 200,        // Proof section is 200vh tall
  progressLagMs: 280,       // Lag/smoothing duration
  progressStart: 0.04,      // When progress starts (4%)
  progressEnd: 0.96,        // When progress ends (96%)
  progressPower: 1.04,      // Easing curve power
},
```

---

### 4. **How Proof Scene Sets Colors (Palette)**

**Static Fallback Color Palette** (`AboutProofRenderer.ts`, lines 14-16):
```typescript
const FALLBACK_COLORS = [
  0x6644aa, 0x4488bb, 0x44aacc, 0x228866, 
  0x886622, 0xaa4466, 0x664488, 0x4466aa,
] as const;
```

**Color Application Logic** (`AboutProofRenderer.ts`, lines 41-64):

1. **Card Material Creation** (lines 41-64):
   ```typescript
   function createCardMaterial(
     texture: THREE.Texture | null,
     color: number,
   ): THREE.MeshBasicMaterial {
     const mat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({
       map: texture ?? null,
       color: texture ? 0xffffff : color,  // White if textured, else use palette color
       side: THREE.DoubleSide,
     });
     // ... shader for UV flipping
     return mat;
   }
   ```

2. **Color Selection During Card Addition** (lines 240-265):
   ```typescript
   private _addCard(
     group: THREE.Group,
     index: number,
     total: number,
     texture: THREE.Texture | null,
     radius: number,
   ): void {
     // ... position/rotation setup
     const mat = createCardMaterial(
       texture,
       FALLBACK_COLORS[index % FALLBACK_COLORS.length],  // Cycles through palette
     );
     this._materials.push(mat);
     const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);
