---

### 6. **Gallery Canvas Scroll Speed Control**

**Key Constants** (`InfiniteGalleryRenderer.ts`, lines 13-30):

| Constant | Value | Purpose |
|----------|-------|---------|
| `SCROLL_DAMPING` | `0.95` | Exponential velocity decay per frame |
| `AUTO_PLAY_ACCEL` | `0.7` | Acceleration when auto-playing |
| `SCROLL_SPEED` | `2.5` | Input multiplier for wheel/touch/keyboard |
| `MAX_SCROLL_VEL` | `40.0` | Maximum velocity cap |
| `IDLE_THRESHOLD_MS` | `3000` | Time before auto-play starts |

**Input Handling & Velocity** (lines 201-229):

```typescript
// Wheel input
this._onWheel = (e) => {
  this._scrollVelocity += e.deltaY * 0.01 * SCROLL_SPEED;  // 2.5x multiplier
  this._scrollVelocity = Math.max(-MAX_SCROLL_VEL, Math.min(MAX_SCROLL_VEL, this._scrollVelocity));
};

// Keyboard input
if (e.key === "ArrowDown" || e.key === "ArrowRight") {
  this._scrollVelocity += 2 * SCROLL_SPEED;  // 5.0 fixed increment
}

// Touch input
const delta = this._touchLastY - y;
this._scrollVelocity += delta * 0.03 * SCROLL_SPEED;  // 0.075x delta multiplier
```

**Physics in Render Loop** (`InfiniteGalleryRenderer.ts`, lines 405-463):

```typescript
private readonly _tick = (): void => {
  const delta = Math.min(clock.getDelta(), MAX_DELTA);  // Frame time capped at 0.1s

  // Frame-rate-independent exponential damping
  this._scrollVelocity *= Math.pow(SCROLL_DAMPING, delta * 60);  // 0.95^(delta*60)
  if (Math.abs(this._scrollVelocity) < 0.0001) this._scrollVelocity = 0;

  if (this._isAutoPlaying) {
    this._scrollVelocity += AUTO_PLAY_ACCEL * delta;  // 0.7 units/sec when idle
    if (this._scrollVelocity > MAX_SCROLL_VEL) this._scrollVelocity = MAX_SCROLL_VEL;
  }

  // Core movement
  for (const record of this._planes) {
    data.z += this._scrollVelocity * delta * 10;  // Distance per frame = velocity * 10
  }
};
```

**Movement Rate Formula:**
```
distancePerFrame = scrollVelocity * deltaTime * 10
```

Example with wheel scroll:
- User scrolls 100px down
- `scrollVelocity += 100 * 0.01 * 2.5 = 2.5` units
- At 60fps: `distance per frame = 2.5 * (1/60) * 10 ≈ 0.417 units`

---

### 7. **Existing Texture/Image Loading Patterns**

**Pattern 1: Static Images with Mipmaps** (`InfiniteGalleryRenderer.ts`, lines 107-126):
```typescript
function loadTexture(
  loader: THREE.TextureLoader,
  url: string,
  renderer: THREE.WebGLRenderer,
): Promise<THREE.Texture | null> {
  return new Promise((resolve) => {
    loader.load(url, (texture) => {
      texture.minFilter = THREE.LinearMipmapLinearFilter;  // ← With mipmaps
      texture.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;
      texture.generateMipmaps = true;
      texture.anisotropy = renderer.capabilities.getMaxAnisotropy();
      resolve(texture);
    }, undefined, () => resolve(null));
  });
}
```

**Pattern 2: Video Textures** (`AboutProofRenderer.ts`, lines 205-223):
```typescript
private _createVideoElement(url: string): HTMLVideoElement {
  const video = document.createElement("video");
  video.src = url;
  video.loop = true;
  video.muted = true;
  video.playsInline = true;
  video.crossOrigin = "anonymous";
  void video.play();
  this._videoElements.push(video);
  return video;
}

private _createVideoTexture(video: HTMLVideoElement): THREE.VideoTexture {
  const texture = new THREE.VideoTexture(video);
  texture.minFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;
  texture.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;
  texture.generateMipmaps = false;
  return texture;
}
```

**Pattern 3: Graceful Fallback** (Both renderers):
- If API fails → use colored fallback cards
- If texture load fails → use material color (no error throw)

**Resource Cleanup** (`AboutProofRenderer.ts`, lines 170-203):
```typescript
dispose(): void {
  this._geometries.forEach((g) => g.dispose());
  this._materials.forEach((m) => m.dispose());
  this._textures.forEach((t) => t.dispose());
  this._videoElements.forEach((v) => {
    v.pause();
    v.src = "";
